      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T03:24:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had just duplicated what SS had done in their original patch: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/2006760 . Is there any additional cost to using a restricted hook other than loosing the ability to unload the module implementing the hook? Separately, given an old comment from Greg here https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/158645321#comment30 , does the desire to keep a hook fixed for the lifetime of the device justify using an RVH?",
